  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a half marathon and doubled the mileage overnight. By week two the shins were burning, and a mate said to just run through it.\n\nKay explained that a spread-out ache along the shin is different from one focal sore spot, which can point to bone stress. That difference decides whether running can carry on.\n\nWhat can help: cutting running back to a level where symptoms stay low, finding the load spike, building calf strength, trying slightly quicker steps (a 5–7% cadence increase), then rebuilding gradually.\n\nGet it checked if there's one spot that's sore to press, pain that builds during runs, or pain at rest, at night or when hopping.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
